const explanations={
'Earnings LTM':['LTM common earnings equal FY2025 plus H1 2026 less H1 2025. Identical six-month periods avoid overlap.','The diluted-share average is reconstructed with half-year weights; it is not the sum of annual and half-year shares.','Calculated EPS can differ from reported EPS through allocation to participating securities and issuer rounding.','A positive comparable earnings base is required for P/E. Negative earnings remain in the financial history.','Transaction effects remain GAAP unless a separately documented after-tax adjustment is entered.'],
'Profitability':['Returns use common earnings and two-point equity or asset averages. They are issuer-comparable proxies, not daily-average disclosures.','ROTE excludes selected intangible equity and can exceed ROE without an improvement in operating earnings.','Efficiency uses GAAP revenue. Issuer tax-equivalent measures may produce a lower expense ratio.','Acquisition-related charges, card credit costs and trading activity can change returns without a persistent change in franchise quality.','Markets and wealth-management banks should also be reviewed in the commercial-peer exclusion sensitivity.'],
'Tangible Book':['Common equity excludes preferred carrying amounts. Preferred par values are not used as carrying amounts.','Straight subtraction deducts goodwill and other intangibles without applying issuer deferred-tax adjustments.','Issuer reported TCE or TBV takes precedence in the selected basis when available. Both versions remain visible.','Book value times a rounded number of end shares is a reconstruction and can differ from exact common equity.','The selected basis should remain consistent when comparing current P/TBV and historical return proxies.'],
'Capital':['The ratios shown are actual standardized CET1, rather than minimum requirements or advanced-approach ratios.','Regulatory capital and accounting tangible common equity use different deduction rules and denominators.','A higher capital ratio alone does not establish greater franchise value or lower credit risk.','RWA composition, stress requirements, acquisition effects and capital distributions can explain cross-bank differences.','The model excludes regulatory and earnings updates released after the fixed information cutoff.'],
'Credit Quality':['Loan totals preserve the selected issuer definition and period. Gross and net loans are kept separate.','Loan allowance excludes an unfunded commitment reserve unless specifically reported within the selected balance.','Net charge-offs require both charge-offs and recoveries. Missing recovery data is not substituted with zero.','The cost-of-risk proxy uses period-end loans and differs from an issuer average-loan charge-off rate.','Capital One card exposures and acquisition accounting make a uniform basis-point stress an analytical comparison, not equal economic severity.'],
'Funding':['Loans and deposits are June 2026 stocks. Net interest income and revenue are twelve-month flows.','The loan-to-deposit ratio is descriptive. Deposit costs, uninsured balances and liquidity composition require separate evidence.','Markets and wealth banks have different funding sources and asset mixes from commercial lenders.','Cash equivalents do not alone establish regulatory liquidity coverage or net stable funding ratios.','A missing funding or cash definition stays unavailable rather than becoming zero.'],
'Shareholder Returns':['Cash dividends and repurchases retain the selected reported payment definitions. Repurchases are not automatically net buybacks.','Per-share dividends can be declared rather than paid; review the selected tag before interpreting them as cash distributions.','Ending shares and diluted average shares serve different purposes. Repurchases do not rewrite historical EPS averages.','Daily market return calculations exclude dividends and therefore differ from total shareholder returns.','Distribution capacity depends on regulatory capital, expected earnings and credit conditions, not only recent cash payments.']};
